|***************************************************************************
| z41c.ibs * IBIS 5.0 Model 
| 8Gb DDR4 SDRAM - Die Revision "R" 
| This Model is valid for Commercial Temperature Range 0C<=Tc<=95C
|
| Valid for DDR4-1600/1866/2133/2400/2666/2933/3200 operation 
| Models *_3200 are applicable for speed grade 3200 Mbps (-062) and below
|
| Part Number       VDD/VDDQ    Architecture   Package
| -----------       --------    ------------   -------
| MT40A2G4SA        1.2V/1.2V   2Gb   x  4     78-Ball FBGA
| MT40A1G8SA        1.2V/1.2V   1Gb   x  8     78-Ball FBGA
| MT40A512M16TB     1.2V/1.2V   512Mb x 16     96-Ball FBGA
| MT40A2G4Z41C      1.2V/1.2V   2Gb   x  4     Bare Die
| MT40A1G8Z41C      1.2V/1.2V   1Gb   x  8     Bare Die
| MT40A512M16Z41C   1.2V/1.2V   512Mb x 16     Bare Die
|***************************************************************************
|
[IBIS Ver]    5.0
[File Name]   z41c.ibs
[Date]        6/19/2022
[File Rev]    2.3
[Source]      From silicon level SPICE model at Micron Technology, Inc.
              For support contact your local Micron FAE/Sales contacts
              (more information at https://www.micron.com/support/sales-network)
|
[Notes]       Revision History:
              Rev 2.3: 6/19/2022
               - Matched C_comp with 4/25/2022 IOCAP measurements:
              Rev 2.2.2: 12/10/2021
               - Fixed PARITY pin x16 Package Component Model
              Rev 2.2.1: 9/1/2021
               - Added bare die component models
              Rev 2.1.1: 4/14/2021
               - Created Industrial Temperature Range Model
              Rev 2.1: 2/2/2021
               - Matched C_comp with 12/15/2020 IOCAP measurements:
               - Added x16 Package Component and Sparse Matrix Package Model
              Rev 2.0: 11/6/2020
               - Matched IV curves with 11/4/2020 measurements
              Rev 1.1: 4/23/2020
               - Corrected typos in this header
               - Models for ALERT, CLKIN and INPUT generated with new sw tool
              Rev 1.0: 4/13/2020
               - Initial pre-silicon model
               - All models were created from z41c SPF netlists.
|
              Notes:
               - The DQ_IN_ODT* models contain assumed input thresholds,
                 the actual threshold values will depend on the VREFDQ
                 level set by training
               - This IBIS file uses the Submodel keyword to model the
                 DDR4 On-die Termination(ODT) characteristics. 
               - The C_comp value in the DQ I/O model is set to match the 
                 input state of the DQ I/O as measured from the HSPICE model.
                 The C_comp value decreases in the DQ/DQS Input ODT models.
               - L_pin values in the Pin sections are loop inductance and 
                 include the mutual inductance to appropriate POWER/GND
                 return paths.  POWER/GND parasitics are modeled in the 
                 Package Models.
               - Typ and slow corner V-t curves in the following DQ* models 
                 are shifted relative to strong corner V-t curve 
                 to contain all 3 corners within appropriate V-t window
|
                 Models        Typ       Slow      V-t duration
                 --------      ------    ------    ------------
                 DQ*_34_3200    -82ps    -210ps     440ps 
                 DQ*_40_3200    -82ps    -210ps     440ps 
                 DQ*_48_3200    -82ps    -210ps     440ps 
                 ALERT          -30ps     -80ps     300ps
|
               - Due to the shift in typ and slow corner, the V-t curves
                 may overlap each other. This does not effect the accuracy 
                 of the IBIS data.
               - The NF_INPUT Model is for Non-functioning INPUT pins in the
                 x8 package
               - The NF_DQ Model is for Non-functioning DQ pins in the
                 x4 package
                 See Micron IBIS Model Quality Report and Quality Checklist 
                 for full IQ details
|                     
